videos.script:
Every app on a phone gets a folder of its own. Nobody else can read it, and when the app is uninstalled, it goes. {{sandbox}}

Inside it, the system has opinions. One folder is backed up to the cloud. Another is a cache the system empties when the disk runs low. {{folders}} Put the student's plan in the wrong one, and one day it is simply gone.

This lesson sorts what goes where. A theme or the last open tab is a small setting, kept as a preference. {{prefs}} The planner's courses and sessions belong in a database, and both platforms ship one: SQLite. {{sqlite}} You will create it, fill it with the week from lesson 1, and ask it for the same total. {{total}}

And a password or a token goes in neither. It goes in the Keychain or the Keystore, which exist for exactly that. {{secrets}}
